# Day 52

## Experiment Title

Automating Testing using Jenkins Pipelines


## Objective

To understand how testing processes can be automated using Jenkins pipelines.


## Theory

Jenkins pipelines support automated testing as part of Continuous Integration workflows. Automated testing helps developers identify errors early during software development and improves application reliability.

Testing stages can be added inside Jenkins pipelines to automatically execute test cases whenever code changes occur in the project repository.


## Requirements

Jenkins

Java Development Kit

GitHub Repository

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Jenkins dashboard.

Access the existing Jenkins pipeline project.

Configure automated testing stages inside the pipeline.

Save the updated pipeline configuration.

Execute the pipeline and observe testing activity.

Verify testing results and pipeline execution logs.


## Output

Automated testing was executed successfully using Jenkins pipelines.

Pipeline stages completed successfully during workflow execution.

Testing results and execution logs were displayed correctly.


## Result

Successfully automated application testing using Jenkins pipelines.
